  "name": "Minimalist",
  "summary": "Clean minimalist massing with warm off-white plaster planes, a charcoal fluted porch portal on the left, recessed horizontal window bands, a cantilevered front balcony, and a timber-accented entrance.",
  "materials": [
   "warm beige stucco plaster",
   "charcoal fluted metal panels",
   "natural teak wood door",
   "dark grey aluminium window frames",
   "frameless glass balcony railing"
  ]
 },
 "notes": [
  "Designed for a 10.1-marla (35x65 ft) north-facing plot in Johar Town under LDA rules with 10 ft front, 7 ft rear, and 5 ft right setbacks (63.3% ground coverage).",
  "The father's bedroom is located on the ground floor with wide, step-free access off the central TV lounge and an attached bathroom.",
  "A dedicated entrance lobby separates guest access to the drawing room and powder room from the family's private lounge and dining areas.",
  "The stacked dog-leg stair in an 8x14.5 ft hall provides a full 3.5 ft clear landing on each level and rises to the roof mumty, with a concrete water tank beside it and an unshaded south-facing roof zone reserved for a 5 kW solar array."
 ],
